  "id": "COMPOUND:4858 - PROTEIN:1642",
  "verbalization": "XL228 is shown to have a target relationship with the proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src through three distinct pathways, all of which converge on the insulin receptor as a common intermediate. The first pathway links XL228 to the insulin receptor via Ligustrone A, which in turn targets the Src kinase. The second pathway connects XL228 to the insulin receptor through 1-O-beta-D-Glucopyranosyl anthranilate, which also targets Src. The third pathway involves N,N-Dimethylacetamide, which also targets Src. These pathways collectively suggest that XL228 exerts its effects through a mechanism that involves the insulin receptor and its downstream targets, including the Src kinase. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong and consistent relationship, suggesting that XL228 may act as a modulator of the Src signaling pathway. The mechanism appears to involve the insulin receptor, which is a well-known mediator of cellular responses to insulin and is frequently implicated in oncogenic processes. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between XL228 and Src, but further investigation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action and to assess potential therapeutic implications.",
